      "body": "## Why?\n\nWith `--enable-return-routed-experts`, sglang saves each token's routed experts in a CPU buffer, one row per KV slot. The buffer is sized for one GPU's KV pool.\n\nWith DCP (decode context parallel) or KV sharding (`--enable-kv-cache-sharding`), KV slot numbers cover every GPU's pool. Slots past the first GPU's pool have no row, so the server crashes.\n\n```text\nExample: DCP 4, each GPU's KV pool holds 64 tokens\n\nKV slots        0 ──────────────────────────────── 271   (4 GPUs' pools)\nbuffer before   0 ──── 67                                (1 GPU's pool)\n                         └─ slot 68 → IndexError → server crashes\nbuffer after    0 ──────────────────────────────── 271\n```\n\nWe hit this on Kimi-K3 with DCP16 during RL, about 20 minutes into the run.\n\n## What?\n\n- Make the buffer cover every KV slot the allocator can hand out:\n  - no DCP, no KV sharding: unchanged\n  - DCP: every DCP rank's pool\n  - KV sharding: every shard's pool\n- Only one function changes: `RunnerIds.capture_token_capacity`. The indexer top-k buffer uses it too, so it gets the same fix.\n- The int16 buffer option that used to be in this PR is now #47833.\n\n## Verification?\n\nA new unit test fills the KV pool and checks that the buffer has exactly one row per slot:\n\n```text\ncase            largest slot   rows before   rows after\nno DCP               67             68            68\nDCP 4               271             68 ✗         272\nKV sharding 4       271             68 ✗         272     (observed, CPU)\n```\n\n## Test?\n\n- `test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_runner_ids.py::test_capture_capacity_covers_widened_allocator_ids`: **observed** passing on CPU. It **observed** failing on `main` for the DCP and KV-sharding cases.\n- All 19 tests in `test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_runner_ids.py`: **observed** passing on CPU.\n- `pre-commit run` on the changed files: **observed** passing.\n- CI: **pending**.\n- GPU run with DCP and routed experts: **pending**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #41408551131](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41408551131)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41408551182](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41408551182)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41408551092](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41408551092)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n\n\n",
